= Hu Hanmin

Another of Sun Yat-sen's closest disciples, Hu Hanmin's career, however, has not been so fruitful in recent years. Implicated in the assassination of Liao Zhongkai in 1925, Hu spent a year in effective exile as a "representative" of the KMT in Moscow, however it seems his time in Russia has only hardened his conviction against the Communist Party. Now, he lacks a base of power and the influence he once had, but he remains a powerful writer and theorist.

